<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Ich bin kurz davor das Retevis in den Müll zu werfen und DMR nicht zu machen  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_confused.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":?" title="Confused"> <br><br>I'm about to throw the Retevis in the trash and not do DMR <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_confused.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":?" title="Confused"></div></blockquote>Is that towards you duplex hotspot ?<br><br>Check the log files under /var/log/pi-star when you try transmitting.<br>You can mail them to me if you want.<br><br>Have you used this hotspot in duplex mode with some other radio ?<br><br>My personal experience with a duplex hotspot and DMR is not the best but we in Sweden has a much smaller 70 cm band too ( Only 432-438 )<br>and we have a duplex space of 2 MHz which is to small without duplex filters.</div></blockquote><br>so the Pi-Star is definitely online<br><br><a href="https://ibb.co/dpsh7H7" class="postlink"><img src="https://i.ibb.co/dpsh7H7/capture-241107-155533.png" class="postimage" alt="Image"></a></div></blockquote>I'm pretty sure that your problem is in the radio interface between the radio and the mmdvm card. <br><br>DMR and duplex hotspots is complex and the timing must be perfect. <br>I never had any problem running other modes like Dstar on duplex but dmr is unstable and timeouts is not unusual<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Thu Nov 07, 2024 4:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
